WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.030
You're walking home at dusk.

2
00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:06.380
On the path ahead, there's a
dark shape: a few broken lines,

3
00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:08.380
some patches of shadow.

4
00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:10.880
Instantly, you see a crouching dog.

5
00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:12.280
You jump back.

6
00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:14.620
Then a streetlight flickers on.

7
00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:15.970
It's a bin bag.

8
00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.190
Your eyes only gave you scraps.

9
00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.160
So where did the rest
of that dog come from?

10
00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:26.340
In this mission, you'll meet Gregory, who
argued that sensory input is often incomplete

11
00:00:26.390 --> 00:00:27.720
or ambiguous.

12
00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:31.110
So your brain makes a best
guess about what is out there.

13
00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.850
It's called a perceptual hypothesis.

14
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.770
And you'll see a cube drawing
your brain can't settle on,

15
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:39.230
flipping between two hypotheses.

16
00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:44.360
Your mission: explain what fills the gaps
in the picture your eyes send your brain.
